{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1545930-questions-on-purview-thematic-focus-and-motifs","id":1545930,"title":"Questions on Purview thematic focus and Motifs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-15T06:00:03-08:00","id":1545930,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Questions on Purview thematic focus and Motifs","content":"Certain Purviews give you the option of narrowing their thematic focus to a single aspect of that Purview, limiting the use of the Purview's Boons and Marvels to only that focus in exchange for gaining a thematically related Motif that can be used for Marvels in any Purview. This typically done with Artistry, Beasts and Passion, but not necessarily; 'Ila of the Ilhm from Scion 2e God has Wild (Desert), which I think is the first only instance of a thematic focus for a Purview other than Artistry, Beasts or Passion in 2e official rules.<br /> <br /> But how do things work when you have multiple thematic foci for the same Purview? Like, for example, Rahmayyu, also from the Ilhm, who has Artistry (Pottery, Weaving).<br /> <br /> 1. Does it just expand the focus of the Purview, or do you have to count it as a separate iteration of the Purview for each focus?<br /> <br /> 2. Does each focus gets its own individual Motif, or is there just one combined Motif for all of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","user":"ChronoRebel","date":". 11-15-2024, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T10:45:11-08:00","id":1546003,"title":"","content":"1) I would probably say the latter. That is, if you want both Beasts (Dog) and Beasts (Cat), you have to acquire something that would give you an additional Purview outright.<br /> 2) In that same vein, though, I'd give you the full benefit; two distinct motifs that you can use on whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/396-mr-rage","name":"Mr Rage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T15:55:35-08:00","id":1546010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Rage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1545930-questions-on-purview-thematic-focus-and-motifs?p=1546003#post1546003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) I would probably say the latter. That is, if you want both Beasts (Dog) and Beasts (Cat), you have to acquire something that would give you an additional Purview outright.<br /> 2) In that same vein, though, I'd give you the full benefit; two distinct motifs that you can use on whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem for 1). Mysteries of the World states Gods can have at most 10 Purviews. But Veles of the Bogovi in Demigod has Beasts (Bears, Wolves, Snakes, Owls), Chaos, Darkness, Death, Deception, Earth, Fertility, Water, Wild. If we count each Beasts focus as separate Purviews that makes 12.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","user":"ChronoRebel","date":". 11-18-2024, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}